    "title": "Clarity Stall Leaves Banks and Exchanges Looking to SEC - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By PYMNTS ,\n7 hours ago Crypto markets lost their big Washington vote Tuesday (Sept. 15). But the more important fight may be the one that finally came out into the open. The Digital Asset Market Clarity Act had been billed as the long-awaited rulebook that could pull cryptocurrency deeper into the regulated U.S. financial system. Its failure to advance, with the procedural vote falling short, sent crypto stocks tumbling and left the industry staring at yet another stretch of operating domestically without comprehensive federal market structure legislation. Read full article",
